ave drafted legislation that recognizes onesies as critical infant wear and aims to prevent their use as political tools:\n\nInfant Onesie Protection Act (IOPA)\n\nPreamble:Recognizing the fundamental role of infant care in society and acknowledging that onesies serve as a primary garment for infants providing comfort, hygiene, and ease of use; and understanding that the politicization of infant attire can lead to undue stress on families and detract from the focus on child welfare, the following legislation is hereby proposed:\nSection 1: Short TitleThis Act may be cited as the "Infant Onesie Protection Act."\n\nSection 2: DefinitionsFor the purposes of this Act:\nOnesie: An all-in-one garment designed for infants, typically covering the torso and snapping at the crotch, intended for ease of changing.\n\nPolitical Tool: Any use of an item in a manner intended to influence public opinion, affect political outcomes, or garner political support.\nSection 3: Recognition of Onesies(a) Onesies are hereby recognized as critical components of infant wear, essential for:\nMaintaining infant hygiene.\nProviding comfort and ease during routine care.\n\nEnsuring safety and warmth for infants.\n(b) The federal, state, and local governments shall acknowledge the importance of onesies in infant care and support their availability and affordability.\nSection 4: Prohibition of Political Use(a) It shall be unlawful for any governmental or political entity to:\nUse onesies in any campaign material, propaganda, or political messaging that could be construed as endorsing or opposing political views or candidates.\nImpose regulations on onesies that serve no purpose other than to make a political statement or influence political behavior.\n\n(b) This includes, but is not limited to:\n\nDesigning onesies with political slogans or symbols for distribution.\nBanning or restricting onesies based on the political connotations associated with their design or color.\nSection 5: Enforcement(a) The Federal Trade Commission (FTC) shall be responsible for monitoring compliance with this Act. Violations may lead to:\nFines for individuals or entities found using onesies as political tools.\n\nPublic admonishment or legal action if necessary.\n(b) Consumer protection agencies at state and local levels shall assist in enforcement and public education regarding this Act.\nSection 6: Educational EffortsThe Department of Health and Human Services (HHS), in collaboration with pediatric and child welfare organizations, shall undertake educational campaigns to inform the public about the importance of onesies in infant care, emphasizing their utility over any potential political symbolism.\n\nSection 7: Effective DateThis Act shall take effect 90 days after its enactment into law.\nSection 8: SeverabilityIf any provision of this Act or the application thereof to any person or circumstance is held invalid, the remainder of the Act and the application of such provision to other persons or circumstances shall not be affected thereby.\nSection 9: Authorization of AppropriationsThere are authorized to be appropriated such sums as may be necessary to carry out this Act.\nThis draft legislation aims to protect the practical use of onesies in infant care from being overshadowed by political agendas, ensuring that the focus remains on child welfare and family convenience.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': []}, 'media': {'inline_media': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Wed Jan 29 21:55:01 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1884700521040163145', 'display_text_range': [14, 294], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 0, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@TheChiefNerd Republicans have drafted